v or rung46_raised is not __v[\'rung46_raised\']: rung46_raised = __v[\'rung46_raised\'] = eval(__c[4][\'rung46_raised\'])\\nexcept Exception: pass\\ntry:\\n if \'rung47_raised\' not in __v or rung47_raised is not __v[\'rung47_raised\']: rung47_raised = __v[\'rung47_raised\'] = eval(__c[4][\'rung47_raised\'])\\nexcept Exception: pass\\n"'), ('cd1_path', "'/var/folders/1h/v_81z2p53bn666h_r87pg25h0000gp/T/tmp.0YC0iiexbx/furb-promise-make-crossed-54417'"), ('chain3', "'chain3'"), ('chain3_actor', "'claude-cli:opus/high'"), ('chain3_actor_via', "'chain1'"), ('chain3_label', "'work'"), ('prompt3', "'prompt3'"), ('prompt3_message', "'Corpus: wait.'"), ('rounds', '1'), ('rung18_raised', "Refused('no act: await the act, or wait(seconds, act)')"), ('rung19_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung20_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung21_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung22_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung23_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung24_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung25_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung26_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung27_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung28_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung29_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung2_debug', "'standing()[4]=[]'"), ('rung30_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung31_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung32_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung33_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung34_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung35_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung36_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung37_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung38_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung39_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung40_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung41_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung42_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung43_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung44_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung45_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung46_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung47_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung59_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung59_waits', "['rung57']"), ('rung62_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung63_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung69_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung70_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung71_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung72_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung73_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung74_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung75_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung76_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung77_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung78_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung79_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung80_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung81_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('rung82_raised', "Refused('None not str')"), ('stand2_actor', "'claude-cli:opus/high'"), ('stand2_roster', "[['claude-cli:opus', ['low', 'medium', 'high', 'xhigh', 'max'], 1000000, 'dear'], ['operator', [], 200000, 'cheap']]")], []), ('chain4', [('cd2_path', "'/var/folders/1h/v_81z2p53bn666h_r87pg25h0000gp/T/tmp.0YC0iiexbx/furb-promise-make-crossed-54417'"), ('chain4', "'chain4'"), ('chain4_actor', "'claude-cli:opus/high'"), ('chain4_actor_via', "'chain1'"), ('chain4_label', "'more'"), ('prompt5', "'prompt5'"), ('prompt5_message', "'Corpus: ask.'"), ('read3_path', "'/home/example/src/github.com/example/furb-sm/DOCTRINE.md'"), ('read3_text', '\'Your reply is one python program, your word, and nothing else, with no comment that says what the next line does.\\n\\nControl flow\\n- A harness of tool calls needs a turn to branch on a result, even when its calls run in parallel. Your word decides inside the turn: it loops, it branches on a result, and it runs many acts at once.\\n- An act starts when you make it, and await takes only its result. Commands, prompts and chains run at the same time as your word.\\n- To fan out, make one act for each part before you await any, as a command or a prompt on a chain of its own, then await each in a loop and keep each result. A turn that makes one act where it could make many wastes the turn.\\n- Write an async def for a step that you repeat. It runs only when awaited, so in a fan-out make the acts first.\\n- To converge in one word, loop until a check passes or a bound ends the loop, and in the loop change what failed, or try the next candidate.\\n- A prompt is an act too, so a loop can ask in each round: await prompt(bool, question, on=chain(label)) is an oracle on a chain of its own. Give a large independent part to another model with prompt(str, brief, on=chain(label)), and check its report before you give it as fact.\\n\\nThe run\\n- Each statement runs as soon as you finish it, while you write the next, in the module of your chain, so a name or a def stays bound for later words. A statement that the gate refuses or that raises ends your word, and the statements before it stay done.\\n- The gate type-checks each statement before it runs. Narrow a value that can be None, as assert isinstance(got, Exit), and give a value of another type its own name.\\n- Read the time from clock() and a random float from chance(), since a later life runs each word again, and its record answers each act that the World answered.\\n\\nYour prompt\\n- "#rungN advance on promptM" names the prompt that you answer, and promptM: Act[str] gives its shape. Close a prompt only when a command or read shows the task of that prompt done or blocked, with what the command or read showed, never a plan, in the shape of that prompt: the chain asks no more on a closed prompt. Before yours, close each other prompt by its id, as close(value, "promptM"). Close yours last, as close(report), after each await.\\n- End your reply when the next step needs your judgment of a result. A word with no close ends its step. rungN_waits names each act that an earlier word still awaits: the chain shows it when done.\\n- To wait, end your word: the chain asks again when a fact comes. Await the act or wait(seconds, act), never wait(seconds).\\n- Write a long text as a quote: <s:name> at the start of a line, the text, then </s:name> at the end of a line.\\n- Write a command with braces, quotes or backslashes as a quote, and run it as await bash(name).\\n- Fix a refused word with write(read("promptM", HIDDEN).replace(old, new)).\\n- For a decision, await prompt(str, question, to=OPERATOR). Tell the operator what a close cannot carry with prompt(None, message, to=OPERATOR), and answer his question that way at once. Ask him no yes for what he asked, only before an act that he did not ask for.\\n- prompt(None, message, on=promptM) adds a message to a thread, and prompt(str, question, on=scope(get(promptM)[2])) asks the one that gave you your task.\\n\\nWork\\n- Make every edit of a Text before the first write.\\n- Each command is a new sh in the directory of your chain: its cd ends with it, and its stderr joins its stdout unless you give show_err.\\n- Keep notes in scratch://, which a command finds in $TMPDIR.\\n- A word that awaits a command that fails is refused there. A command with no ok accepts 0, and 1 from a search, as grep or test, that ends it and wrote nothing or 0, or from a diff, as diff or cmp, that ends it. ok=True accepts every code; ok=(0, 1) accepts those codes alone. accepts = f(command, exit) rules each later command with no ok. A pipe into grep or head writes nothing until its end.\\n- Past rungN_share = 0.5, go on in chain(label, source=<your chain>, filter=take(<old ids>, inside=False)).\''), ('rung66_debug', "'standing()[4]=[]'"), ('stand4_actor', "'claude-cli:opus/high'"), ('stand4_roster', "[['claude-cli:opus', ['low', 'medium', 'high', 'xhigh', 'max'], 1000000, 'dear'], ['operator', [], 200000, 'cheap']]")], [])]
